{
  "net": "hermann-brain",
  "model": "hermann",
  "session": "agent-hermann",
  "description": "The brain: a curated, bounded model of the project kept from what reality produces. After every merge a script collects the signals (coder notes, review, verification, diff, scorecard) and rebuilds the component map; a curator (a one-shot model call, or a headless agent in curate mode, chosen by config.brainAgent) answers a contract: facts to add and retire, the plan, decisions to propose, questions for the person; a script applies it deterministically. Every brief reads the brain.",
  "places": {
    "p-hermann-brain-cmd": "Brain commands (observe, curate, apply, answer)",
    "p-hermann-brain-log": "Brain command results",
    "p-hermann-signals": "Signals per merged run",
    "p-hermann-context": "Briefs for the judgement lanes",
    "p-hermann-curation": "Curations (the curator's answer)",
    "p-hermann-knowledge": "Knowledge facts: kind, scope, source, confidence, active or retired",
    "p-hermann-map": "Component map per commit (measured)",
    "p-hermann-plan": "The plan: remaining increments toward the goal",
    "p-hermann-adr": "Architecture decision records (the brain proposes, the person decides)",
    "p-hermann-prompts": "Questions for the person",
    "p-hermann-responses": "The person's answers",
    "p-hermann-runs": "Runs",
    "p-hermann-llm-errors": "Answers that missed their contract",
    "p-hermann-journal": "Journal",
    "p-hermann-curations": "Curation archive (every curation as answered, kept)"
  },
  "transitions": [
    {
      "id": "t-hermann-observe-cmd",
      "kind": "command",
      "label": "Observe: signals of a merged run, component map",
      "reads": {
        "input": {
          "place": "p-hermann-brain-cmd",
          "arcql": "FROM $ WHERE $.stage == \"observe\" LIMIT 1"
        },
        "runs": {
          "place": "p-hermann-runs",
          "arcql": "FROM $ LIMIT 1",
          "consume": false,
          "optional": true
        }
      },
      "writes": {
        "log": {
          "place": "p-hermann-brain-log",
          "retain": 200
        },
        "signals": "p-hermann-signals",
        "map": "p-hermann-map",
        "context": "p-hermann-context",
        "brain_cmd": "p-hermann-brain-cmd",
        "journal": "p-hermann-journal"
      },
      "emit": [
        {
          "from": "@result",
          "to": "log"
        }
      ],
      "command": {
        "timeoutMs": 600000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t-hermann-curate",
      "kind": "agent",
      "label": "Curate (one-shot model call)",
      "reads": {
        "ctx": {
          "place": "p-hermann-context",
          "arcql": "FROM $ WHERE $.purpose == \"curate\" LIMIT 1",
          "ttl": 600000
        }
      },
      "writes": {
        "curation": "p-hermann-curation",
        "errors": {
          "place": "p-hermann-llm-errors",
          "retain": 100
        },
        "archive": {
          "place": "p-hermann-curations",
          "retain": 50
        }
      },
      "agent": {
        "role": "r",
        "tier": "medium",
        "maxIterations": 1,
        "oneShot": true,
        "autoEmit": true,
        "allowedTools": [],
        "answerSchema": {
          "required": [
            "curationId",
            "runId",
            "addFacts",
            "plan",
            "summary"
          ],
          "types": {
            "addFacts": "array",
            "plan": "object",
            "summary": "string"
          },
          "retries": 1
        },
        "nl": "You are Hermann's brain, curating what the project knows after one merged iteration. Read the brief, then reply with ONE JSON object and nothing else.\n\n${ctx.data.brief}\n\nRules: facts must be specific and sourced from the brief (a class, a config key, a package, a measured number); prefer few good facts over many; mark as platform what is true for the stack and reusable in other projects, as project what is about this codebase; propose a decision for every choice the coder made that constrains future work; keep the plan as the remaining increments toward the goal in dependency order, marking what is merged; ask a question only when the next increment genuinely depends on the answer. Always include every array, empty when there is nothing.\n\nReply with exactly this shape: {\"curationId\": \"<from the brief>\", \"runId\": \"<from the brief>\", \"addFacts\": [{\"kind\": \"platform|convention|decision|gap|risk|question\", \"scope\": \"project|platform\", \"text\": \"<one specific, checkable sentence>\", \"source\": \"<runId, specId or file>\", \"confidence\": \"high|medium|low\"}], \"retireFacts\": [\"<factId>\"], \"plan\": {\"increments\": [{\"id\": \"inc-1\", \"title\": \"<one line>\", \"status\": \"planned|in-progress|merged|dropped\", \"dependsOn\": [\"inc-0\"], \"specId\": \"<specId or empty>\"}]}, \"proposedDecisions\": [{\"title\": \"<short>\", \"context\": \"<why it came up>\", \"decision\": \"<what was decided>\", \"consequences\": \"<what it constrains>\"}], \"questions\": [{\"question\": \"<what only the person can answer>\", \"why\": \"<what depends on it>\"}], \"summary\": \"<three sentences>\"}"
      },
      "emit": [
        {
          "from": "@response",
          "to": "archive",
          "when": "summary != ''"
        },
        {
          "from": "@response",
          "to": "curation",
          "when": "summary != ''"
        },
        {
          "from": "@response",
          "to": "errors",
          "when": "summary == ''"
        },
        {
          "from": "@response",
          "to": "errors",
          "when": "error"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "t-hermann-curate-cmd",
      "kind": "command",
      "label": "Curate (headless agent, may read the repository)",
      "reads": {
        "input": {
          "place": "p-hermann-brain-cmd",
          "arcql": "FROM $ WHERE $.stage == \"curate\" LIMIT 1"
        }
      },
      "writes": {
        "log": {
          "place": "p-hermann-brain-log",
          "retain": 200
        },
        "curation": "p-hermann-curation",
        "archive": {
          "place": "p-hermann-curations",
          "retain": 50
        }
      },
      "emit": [
        {
          "from": "@result",
          "to": "log"
        }
      ],
      "command": {
        "timeoutMs": 1800000
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t-hermann-apply-prep",
      "kind": "map",
      "label": "Curation to apply command",
      "reads": {
        "cur": {
          "place": "p-hermann-curation",
          "arcql": "FROM $ LIMIT 1"
        }
      },
      "writes": {
        "cmd": "p-hermann-brain-cmd"
      },
      "template": {
        "kind": "command",
        "id": "apply-${now()}",
        "executor": "script",
        "command": "invoke",
        "expect": "text",
        "stage": "apply",
        "curationId": "${cur.data.curationId}",
        "filedAt": "${now()}",
        "args": {
          "toolId": "hermann-brain",
          "argv": [
            "apply",
            "${cur.data.curationId}"
          ],
          "env": {
            "MODEL_ID": "hermann",
            "CURATION_ID": "${cur.data.curationId}",
            "RUN_ID": "${cur.data.runId}"
          },
          "timeoutMs": 300000
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t-hermann-answer-knowledge-prep",
      "kind": "map",
      "label": "A person's answer to a brain question",
      "reads": {
        "resp": {
          "place": "p-hermann-responses",
          "arcql": "FROM $ WHERE $.intent == \"knowledge\" LIMIT 1"
        }
      },
      "writes": {
        "cmd": "p-hermann-brain-cmd"
      },
      "template": {
        "kind": "command",
        "id": "answer-${now()}",
        "executor": "script",
        "command": "invoke",
        "expect": "text",
        "stage": "answer",
        "promptId": "${resp.data.promptId}",
        "filedAt": "${now()}",
        "args": {
          "toolId": "hermann-brain",
          "argv": [
            "answer",
            "${resp.data.promptId}"
          ],
          "env": {
            "MODEL_ID": "hermann",
            "PROMPT_ID": "${resp.data.promptId}",
            "ANSWER_TEXT": "${resp.data.text}"
          },
          "timeoutMs": 120000
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "t-hermann-apply-cmd",
      "kind": "command",
      "label": "Apply: knowledge, plan, proposed decisions, questions",
      "reads": {
        "input": {
          "place": "p-hermann-brain-cmd",
          "arcql": "FROM $ WHERE $.stage == \"apply\" OR $.stage == \"answer\" LIMIT 1"
        },
        "archive": {
          "place": "p-hermann-curations",
          "arcql": "FROM $ LIMIT 1",
          "consume": false,
          "optional": true
        }
      },
      "writes": {
        "log": {
          "place": "p-hermann-brain-log",
          "retain": 200
        },
        "knowledge": "p-hermann-knowledge",
        "plan": "p-hermann-plan",
        "adr": "p-hermann-adr",
        "prompts": "p-hermann-prompts",
        "journal": "p-hermann-journal"
      },
      "emit": [
        {
          "from": "@result",
          "to": "log"
        }
      ],
      "command": {
        "timeoutMs": 300000
      }
    }
  ]
}
